148 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The advent of Artificial Intelligence \(AI\) has been a double-edged sword. On one hand, it has ushered in an era of unprecedented technological advancement, automating complex tasks, and providing insightful data analysis that was previously impossible. Industries from healthcare to finance are leveraging AI to improve efficiency and accuracy. For instance, AI algorithms can detect diseases from medical scans with greater precision than the human eye. On the other hand, the rise of AI poses significant ethical and societal challenges. Job displacement is a major concern, as machines begin to perform tasks traditionally done by humans. Furthermore, issues of data privacy and the potential for algorithmic bias are critical hurdles that society must navigate. An AI system trained on biased data will perpetuate and even amplify existing societal prejudices, leading to unfair outcomes in areas like hiring and loan applications. Ensuring the responsible development and deployment of AI is paramount to harnessing its benefits while mitigating its risks.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
